\f1\fs22 I will be healed; save me and I will be saved, for you are the one I praise.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Stand at the crossroads and look; ask for the ancient paths, where the good way is, and walk in it, and you will find rest for your souls.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>give birth to a son, and will call him Immanuel.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>and the government will be on his shoulders. And he will be called Wonderful Counsellor,\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>plans to prosper you and not to harm you, plans to give you hope and a future.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>they shall mount up with wings like eagles, they shall run and not be weary, they shall walk and not faint.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>But he was pierced for our transgressions, he was crushed for our iniquities; the punishment that brought us peace was on him, and by his wounds we are healed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
\ul <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He has sent me to bind up the brokenhearted, to proclaim freedom for the captives and release from darkness for the prisoners\ulnone \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>I will answer you and tell you great and unsearchable things you do not know.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
\ul <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>You will seek me and find me when you seek me with all your heart.\ulnone \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>How you have fallen from heaven, morning star, son of the dawn! You have been cast down to the earth, you who once laid low the nations!\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Look to the rock from which you were cut and to the quarry from which you were hewn\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
\ul <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>prepare the way for the Lord; make straight in the desert a highway for our God\ulnone \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Come, all you who are thirsty, come to the waters; and you who have no money, come, buy and eat! Come, buy wine and milk without money and without cost\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Here is my servant, whom I uphold, my chosen one in whom I delight; I will put my Spirit on him, and he will bring justice to the nations.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The wolf will live with the lamb, the leopard will lie down with the goat, the calf and the lion and the yearling together; and a little child will lead them.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>I will sing for the one I love a song about his vineyard: My loved one had a vineyard on a fertile hillside.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>I will create new heavens and a new earth. The former things will not be remembered, nor will they come to mind.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He was despised and rejected by others, a man of suffering, and familiar with pain. Like one from whom people hide their faces he was despised, and we held him in low esteem.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The grass withers and the flowers fall, but the word of our God endures forever.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>I will make it a wasteland, neither pruned nor cultivated, and briers and thorns will grow there. I will command the clouds not to rain on it.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>These people come near to me with their mouth and honor me with their lips, but their hearts are far from me. Their worship of me is based on merely human rules they have been taught.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Call to me and I will answer you and tell you great and unsearchable things you do not know.\
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

